<title>THAILAND: Thai passenger car imports tumble in October.</title>
<headline>Thai passenger car imports tumble in October.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's passenger car imports in October fell to 1,539 units from 4,328 in the same month last year, the Customs Department said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It did not give a reason for the sharp fall.</p>
<p>Tax collection on car imports in October totalled 862.9 million baht ($34.5 million) compared with 4.33 billion baht in in the same month of 1995, the department said in a statement.</p>
<p>European cars were the largest import with 882 units, and South Korea was second with 291, it said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
